# Obsidian — vault root is projects/
# The config is tracked so the vault is reproducible; these two churn constantly.
projects/.obsidian/workspace.json
projects/.obsidian/workspace-mobile.json
projects/.obsidian/cache

# Community plugin code and settings. Excluded BEFORE the first plugin is
# installed, deliberately: a plugin's data.json holds its settings, and for a
# sync plugin that means the server URI, username and password. This repo's
# never-write list bars credentials at any visibility, and git history is
# permanent — so the ordering matters more than the rule. Added 2026-08-12,
# ahead of Self-hosted LiveSync.
# community-plugins.json stays tracked: it names which plugins to install,
# which is the reproducibility that matters, and it holds no secrets.
projects/.obsidian/plugins/*

# Exception, added 2026-08-16: `command-center` is first-party source written in
# this repo, not an installed community plugin, so losing it on a fresh checkout
# would lose real work. The rule above was always about the second kind.
# The credential reasoning is untouched — data.json is still excluded explicitly,
# and this plugin has no settings to write one. node_modules is build input.
# Note `plugins/*` rather than `plugins/`: git cannot re-include anything beneath
# an excluded *directory*, so the glob has to exclude the children instead.
!projects/.obsidian/plugins/command-center/
projects/.obsidian/plugins/command-center/node_modules/
projects/.obsidian/plugins/command-center/data.json

# macOS
.DS_Store

# Syncthing — this repo is a Syncthing folder (Mac <-> homelab over Tailscale).
# .stignore excludes /.git from sync, so history travels via `origin`, not Syncthing.
.stfolder/
.stignore
.stversions/

# Python bytecode. Untracked after a .pyc was swept into a commit on
# 2026-08-12 by an over-broad `git add -A`.
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# Raw financial exports (Monarch Money CSVs). Derived data: re-exportable from
# the source at any time, churns on every pull, and a full transaction ledger is
# the most sensitive thing this repo could hold. Git history is permanent, so the
# exports stay out of it and only the conclusions drawn from them get committed.
# The README is tracked so the convention survives an empty folder.
# Added 2026-08-13, when Monarch was first connected.
# NOTE: Syncthing still replicates these to the homelab — .stignore excludes only
# /.git. Gitignoring keeps them out of history, not off the other machine.
projects/finances/data/*
!projects/finances/data/README.md

# The Reminders sync's run reports. Derived from the workspace on every run, so
# committing one would version a snapshot of state git already holds. The
# sharper reason is what a report *is*: a single flat list of every actionable
# item at once, health-grade domains included. No entry in it is new, and the
# assembly is — the same aggregation argument that makes the systems map and the
# deep-research effort private. The manifest carries a `private` rule as well,
# because gitignoring keeps it out of history and the manifest keeps it out of
# the export, and neither substitutes for the other.
.scratch/reminders-sync/

# The dashboard's rendered output. Derived from the workspace on every build, so
# committing it would version a snapshot of state that git already holds — and
# it churns on every scan. The builder and its template are tracked; the build
# is not.
tools/dashboard/dist/

# lms-publish leaves no state; only bytecode
tools/lms-publish/__pycache__/
